"Protected Materials" means the Software and Documentation collectively,
including their copyrightable selection, arrangement, structure, expression,
and original visual implementation.

"ContentFlow Method Expression" means the specific copyrightable expression,
documentation, schemas, naming, arrangement, and implementation in the
Protected Materials concerning the eight Universal Processes, four Essential
Blocks, three Operators, interfaces, execution contracts, and plugin ecosystem.
It does not claim copyright in abstract ideas, procedures, systems, methods, or
concepts to the extent those are excluded from copyright protection by law.

"Plugin" means independently developed software that interoperates with an
unmodified authorized copy of ContentFlow exclusively through a documented
plugin API, SDK, manifest, protocol, command, or other interoperability surface
published by the Licensor.

"Derivative Product" means software, documentation, or a service based on,
adapted from, translated from, or incorporating a material portion of the
Protected Materials.

"Competitive Product" means a Derivative Product, or a product developed using
the Protected Materials, whose primary purpose substantially reproduces,
replaces, or competes with the ContentFlow core application, its visual
method builder, its project execution environment, its strategic library, or
its plugin management platform. A bona fide Plugin is not a Competitive Product.

"Rebranding" or "Reskinning" means presenting the Software or a Derivative
Product as a different product mainly by changing its name, trademarks, text,
colors, typography, icons, layout, styling, or other superficial presentation
while retaining a material part of the Protected Materials or their
implementation.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
License, including any person directing an automated system or artificial
intelligence tool to act on its behalf.

"Third-Party Materials" means dependencies, libraries, fonts, icons, media, or
other materials identified as belonging to third parties and governed by their
