4. PLUGIN ECOSYSTEM EXCEPTION

You may create, use, publish, sell, and license a Plugin if all of the following
conditions are met:

a. The Plugin interoperates through documented ContentFlow extension
   surfaces and does not incorporate, copy, translate, or derive from the core
   implementation, except for unmodified public protocol/type declarations
   strictly necessary for interoperability.

b. The Plugin does not replace the ContentFlow core, bypass licensing or
   security controls, or recreate a substantial part of the core interfaces,
   method builder, execution engine, strategic library, or plugin manager.

c. The Plugin has its own license, accurately declares permissions, data
   handling, external providers, costs, and side effects, and complies with the
   ContentFlow plugin protocol applicable to its declared API version.

d. The Plugin does not use ContentFlow names, logos, or visual identity as
   its own and does not imply sponsorship or endorsement. Truthful nominative
   wording such as "compatible with ContentFlow" is permitted.

e. The Plugin preserves all notices and attribution required by any public SDK
   or protocol files it lawfully includes.

This exception is intentionally designed to support an honest plugin ecosystem.
It does not authorize a fork, alternative distribution, white-label version,
hosted clone, or replacement for ContentFlow.

