b. Create, operate, publish, distribute, or assist in creating a Derivative
   Product or Competitive Product from the Protected Materials.

c. Rebrand, reskin, white-label, rename, recolor, restyle, or superficially
   modify the Software or a Derivative Product and present it as a new or
   independent product.

d. Offer the Software or a Derivative Product as software-as-a-service, a hosted
   service, managed service, marketplace product, template, starter kit, or
   commercial/internal platform for third parties.

e. Extract, copy, or use material portions of the source code, Documentation,
   interface implementation, schemas, or ContentFlow Method Expression to
   reproduce the core product in another codebase, framework, language, or
   visual design.

f. Circumvent the plugin architecture, permission system, license notices,
   attribution, security controls, feature restrictions, or technical measures.

g. Remove, hide, alter, or falsify copyright, authorship, trademark, provenance,
   or license notices.

h. Use ContentFlow trademarks, names, domains, logos, or confusingly similar
   identifiers as the name or branding of another product or service.

i. Represent that a fork, derivative, or Plugin is official, approved, or
   maintained by the Licensor without written authorization.

j. Use the Protected Materials as a dataset to train, fine-tune, benchmark for
