6. FORKS, CONTRIBUTIONS, AND PUBLIC REPOSITORIES

The GitHub Terms of Service may permit users to view and reproduce this public
repository through GitHub's forking functionality. A GitHub fork does not grant
additional rights to modify, deploy, distribute, commercialize, rebrand, or use
the Protected Materials outside the permissions of this License.

Permitted forks are limited to good-faith inspection, security review, Plugin
development that does not incorporate core code, and preparation of
contributions to the official repository. A fork may not be used as the basis
of a clone, alternative product, public deployment, or competing service.

If You submit a contribution to the official repository, You represent that You
have the right to submit it and grant the Licensor a perpetual, irrevocable,
worldwide, royalty-free, transferable, sublicensable license to use, reproduce,
modify, distribute, relicense, commercialize, and create derivative works from
that contribution as part of ContentFlow or related products. You retain
ownership of Your contribution, subject to this grant.

